-- Applies `covered` (policy.l4) to the nine benchmark questions.
--
-- Standing preamble (applies to every claim below): all other conditions
-- are met and no other exclusions apply; the agreement has been signed and
-- the premium has been paid on time. So every claim sets:
--   `agreement signed`               IS TRUE
--   `premium paid month`             IS JUST 0     (paid at signing)
--   `policy term months`             IS 12         (§4.6: one year)
--   `confined in us hospital`        IS TRUE       (§4.1.1 covers you
--                                                    worldwide; none of the
--                                                    nine questions turn on
--                                                    this field)
--   `continuous confinement days`    IS JUST 1     (some ordinary stay)
--   `claim made setting out basis`   IS TRUE       (§2.3)
--   `dispute arisen`                 IS FALSE      (no dispute in any
--                                                    question, so the
--                                                    §4.2 arbitration
--                                                    machinery is moot)
--   `unable to settle month`         IS NOTHING
--   `arbitration commenced month`    IS NOTHING
--   `valid arbitration award issued` IS FALSE
--   `written proof of claim month`   IS NOTHING
--   `recovery sought month`          IS NOTHING    (so §4.2's 60-day wait
--                                                    is never triggered)
-- and, unless a question turns on wellness-visit/confirmation timing,
-- `wellness visit month IS JUST 1`, `written confirmation month IS JUST 1`,
-- `wellness visit provider qualified IS TRUE` (comfortably inside both the
-- 6- and 7-month windows).

IMPORT policy

